.\" help2man include for imud-status.1 — the hand-written sections.
.\" OPTIONS is generated from `imud-status --help`; everything else lives here.
.\" See tools/man-postprocess.py and `make docs-man`.

[NAME]
imud\-status \- query imud daemon health and sensor status

[SYNOPSIS]
.B imud-status
\&[\fB\-\-socket\fR \fIPATH\fR]

[DESCRIPTION]
.B imud-status
connects to the running
.BR imud (8)
daemon over a Unix domain socket, requests a status snapshot, and prints a
formatted summary to stdout.
.PP
The summary includes:
.PP
.RS 4
\(bu\ \ IMU and magnetometer driver names and sample rates
.br
\(bu\ \ MEKF convergence state
.br
\(bu\ \ Calibration flags (gyro, accel, magnetometer)
.br
\(bu\ \ Output stream status (NMEA, high-rate)
.br
\(bu\ \ Current heading, pitch, and roll
.br
\(bu\ \ Declination and true heading (when available)
.RE
.PP
Exits immediately after printing one snapshot.
For a continuous live display use
.BR imud-mon (1).

[EXIT STATUS]
.B 0
on success,
.B 1
if the daemon is not reachable.

[PERMISSIONS]
The status socket is mode 0660, owner
.IR imud:imud ,
so an ordinary user must be in the
.I imud
group to query it:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
sudo adduser "$USER" imud
.EE
.RE
.PP
Log out and back in for the new group to take effect, or run
.B imud-status
under
.BR sudo .

[EXAMPLES]
.EX
imud-status
.EE

[SEE ALSO]
.BR imud (8),
.BR imud-mon (1)

[AUTHOR]
Richard Simpson
